{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1132650-is-there-a-dream-eater-or-ravager-antagonist-or-otherwise-in-1st-edition","id":1132650,"title":"Is there a Dream eater or ravager antagonist or otherwise in 1st edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-22T09:14:50-07:00","id":1132650,"title":"Is there a Dream eater or ravager antagonist or otherwise in 1st edition?","content":"If so where are they? I am looking for rules about a creature that needs to eat dreams to survive. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14195-kallarah","name":"Kallarah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T09:33:47-07:00","id":1132659,"title":"","content":"Define &quot;eat dreams&quot;? Whole dreams, some of the Flora or fauna of dreams, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T09:36:55-07:00","id":1132662,"title":"","content":"I am thinking whole dreams. I am thinking of something that is like a Tremere lich but instead of souls, they eat dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14195-kallarah","name":"Kallarah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T12:59:00-07:00","id":1132755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallarah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1132650-is-there-a-dream-eater-or-ravager-antagonist-or-otherwise-in-1st-edition?p=1132662#post1132662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am thinking whole dreams. I am thinking of something that is like a Tremere lich but instead of souls, they eat dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well... dreams are usually easier to come by than souls. It is either going to have minimal impact (only affecting a single target over a prolonged span of time), or it is going to need to upgrade that to eating the <i>capacity</i> for dreams as well (at least for a time). Or be an explosive breeder, or have some other sort of consequence.<br /> <br /> What is the story goal for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T16:40:25-07:00","id":1132838,"title":"","content":"Dancers in the Dusk has a whole section on Incubi. I don't know if any of them exactly fit what you're looking for but Goblin Miners and Night Hags both disrupt dreams to steal willpower. They don't per-say eat the dream but it's a similar concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T19:08:24-07:00","id":1132886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1132650-is-there-a-dream-eater-or-ravager-antagonist-or-otherwise-in-1st-edition?p=1132755#post1132755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well... dreams are usually easier to come by than souls. It is either going to have minimal impact (only affecting a single target over a prolonged span of time), or it is going to need to upgrade that to eating the <i>capacity</i> for dreams as well (at least for a time). Or be an explosive breeder, or have some other sort of consequence.<br /> <br /> What is the story goal for this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One of my players, who is a fairest, undertook an epic quest to redeem her uncle who is a Tremere and she traveled to the 6th Watchtower through his dreams. Unfortunately, rather than redeem him, she gave her name to the Watchtower. I am trying to figure out what the consequences are going to be for that, but I was thinking of making her crave something that she is now lacking to sustain her existence. I was thinking dreams, but it really could be anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14195-kallarah","name":"Kallarah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T20:12:29-07:00","id":1132894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallarah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1132650-is-there-a-dream-eater-or-ravager-antagonist-or-otherwise-in-1st-edition?p=1132886#post1132886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> One of my players, who is a fairest, undertook an epic quest to redeem her uncle who is a Tremere and she traveled to the 6th Watchtower through his dreams. Unfortunately, rather than redeem him, she gave her name to the Watchtower. I am trying to figure out what the consequences are going to be for that, but I was thinking of making her crave something that she is now lacking to sustain her existence. I was thinking dreams, but it really could be anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>How would she reach the 6th (or 7th?) Watchtower through his dreams? Wouldn't that just be a dream version? Isn't it in the Abyss?</li> <li>If she signed her name to a Watchtower, wouldn't that make her a Mage? Or a weird Mage-Changeling hybrid?</li> <li>If she signed on the soul-eating Watchtower, why not have her simply eat souls? Perhaps via Dreams, because, you know, Changeling and all.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Having your dream-form killed can trigger the Soul-Shocked Condition, right? I'd think it being done by a nascent soul-eater might lead to more permanent consequences.</li> </ol></li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T10:31:31-07:00","id":1133071,"title":"","content":"Thanks Vent0! I think I figured out how I want to run this. I am going to have her eat souls while she harvest emotions or does damage in dream combat. She is going to do willpower damage to her victims and if she drops them to 0 she will completely consume the soul, causing all of the negatives for the individual there. She can decide if she feels guilty or not and live with the Clarity checks haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14195-kallarah","name":"Kallarah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T16:44:09-07:00","id":1133212,"title":"","content":"Not 1e, but likely compatible are David Hill's Cambions, they are dream eaters, anyone who sleeps near them don't dream.<br /> <br /> They also eat Glamour.<br /> <br /> They are the childern of dream fae and a human, hybrids.<br /> <br /> They are also hard to kill, you have to cut off their heads or burn them to be sure as they don't need air, water, food, and they can't bleed to death.<br /> <br /> I don't even think you have to change their stats to use them in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}